<title>BELGIUM: EU vets C&amp;W/BCE joint control of Videotron.</title>
<headline>EU vets C&amp;W/BCE joint control of Videotron.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it was starting a preliminary inquiry into the acquisition by Cable &amp; Wireless Plc and BCE Inc of the joint control of Bell Cablemedia Plc and Videotron Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>It said the deal was notified for clearance under the European Union's merger regulation 4064/89 on November 8.</p>
<p>Under the regulation, which bans creation or strengthening of a dominant position in the Union's market, the Commission has about one month from notification to clear the operation or start a full probe.</p>
<p>British companies Bell Cablemedia and Videotron build and operate cable television and telecomunication networks, the Commission said in a statement to be published in the Official Journal.</p>
<p>Bell Cablemedia is currently owned by Bell Canada International, itself a unit of telecommunications firm BCE Inc. Videotron belongs to Videotron Groupe Ltee also of Canada.</p>
</text>
